<title>FRANCE: CIC constituent bank 1996 profit details.</title>
<headline>CIC constituent bank 1996 profit details.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a table of 1996 net consolidated results for the regional banks which make up the French CIC banking group, part of state insurer GAN and due to be privatised this year.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>Those whose have been making a profit previously:</p>
<p>    Banque CIAL				    306  up 10 percent</p>
<p>    Banque CIO				     106  up  3 percent</p>
<p>    Banque Regionale de l'Ouest		 61  up 21 percent</p>
<p>    Banque Scalbert Dupont			53  up 82 percent</p>
<p>    Banque SNVB				    127  up 11 percent</p>
<p>    Lyonnaise de Banque			  144  up 19 percent</p>
<p>Those who are &quot;making a comeback or pulling out of trouble&quot;</p>
<p>    Banque CIN			    profit  40  vs loss 8 in '95</p>
<p>    Banque Regionale de l'Ain		    1  vs  not given</p>
<p>    CIC Paris					 18  vs  total loss</p>
<p>								    of 163 in</p>
<p>							    two previous years</p>
<p>    Societe Bordelaise			    17  vs loss of 70</p>
<p>								million in 1994</p>
<p>NOTE: Source - CIC group results documents</p>
<p>Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
